<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (Breast cancer is one of the most common cancers affecting women worldwide, and early, accurate diagnosis significantly improves treatment outcomes. Machine learning offers a powerful way to support clinical decision-making by learning patterns from diagnostic measurements that are difficult for the human eye to weigh consistently across thousands of cases.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
90 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (This report documents an end-to-end supervised learning project built on the Breast Cancer Wisconsin \(Diagnostic\) dataset. The goal is to classify a tumor as malignant or benign using measurements derived from digitized images of a fine needle aspirate \(FNA\) of a breast mass. The project follows a complete workflow: understanding the data, cleaning and preparing it, exploring it visually and statistically, training multiple classification algorithms, and rigorously comparing their performance.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
