/E (The dataset used is the Breast Cancer Wisconsin \(Diagnostic\) Dataset, originally hosted on the UCI Machine Learning Repository and made available through Scikit-learn's built-in dataset loader \(sklearn.datasets.load_breast_cancer\). It is a well-known benchmark dataset for binary classification tasks in the medical domain.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 67 0 R
/E (Each record contains 30 numeric features computed from a digitized image of an FNA of a breast mass. These describe characteristics of cell nuclei present in the image - radius, texture, perimeter, area, smoothness, compactness, concavity, concave points, symmetry, and fractal dimension - each reported as a mean, standard error, and 'worst' \(largest\) value, giving 10 x 3 = 30 total features.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
