/E (10.1 Best Model and Justification)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 76 0 R
/E (Logistic Regression achieved the best overall performance, with a test accuracy of 98.25% and the highest ROC-AUC among all six models \(effectively tied with SVM\). Both are strong candidates because, once features are standardized, the two diagnostic classes are close to linearly separable, which plays directly to the strengths of a linear model like Logistic Regression and a well-tuned RBF-kernel SVM. Both models also showed the best balance of precision and recall, which matters greatly in a medical context where both false positives \(unnecessary alarm\) and false negatives \(missed cancer\) carry real costs.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
